  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 222 AM EDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nThe upper trough that's been the main synoptic feature the past \ncouple of days is finally going to pass its central axis overhead \ntoday. As such, some wraparound scattered showers will be again \npossible today, but overall amounts will be negligible. Expecting \nplenty of clouds around too, with the saturated lower third of the \natmosphere.\n\nThe only thing to watch will be any high water coming across the \nmountains via the rivers. The Pigeon River at Newport is forecast to \nrise to action stage by this evening thanks to heavy rainfall on the \nNorth Carolina mountains. This is not a Helene repeat, thankfully, \nbut still caution is warranted near the river.\n\nOtherwise we earn another mild October week again with a strong \nsouthern 500 mb ridge powering temperatures back into the 80s each \nday Monday through Thursday with no rain chances. Late week Friday \ninto Saturday low rain chances return as there's growing indications \nof a decent cold front coming to knock temperatures down a peg or \ntwo. As of right now no significant weather concerns there.",
